# The appliance's own approved destinations in connected mode ("approved destinations only"). Ships
# with the image and can't be removed on the appliance; the office adds its own with
# suveryn-network-mode allow <domain>. One domain per line; a domain also covers its subdomains.

# Sūveryn Labs: the portal, updates and model bundles.
suveryn.com

# Model downloads (suveryn-core models/manifest.json): Hugging Face and the hosts its downloads redirect to.
huggingface.co
hf.co

# Ubuntu's security updates: for the legacy Packer test image only. The read-only (mkosi) image has no
# apt; its fixes come as sūveryn updates (decision D3, tracker #40). It ships this same file, so these two
# names are approved there too, unused, until the Packer image is retired (tracker #60).
security.ubuntu.com
archive.ubuntu.com

# Time, when the office has no time server of its own.
ntp.ubuntu.com
